@julien92git just scroll down or search/filter versions, there also 2.10 and 3.0.0rc1 etc

"Strange" numbers it's a "randomized" tag (kind of hash of image) because images built frequently from source code, probably after every Github commit.

Docker initially is a tool for developers, for quick deploy and testing with various environments.

I’ve got a similar setup.
Running the non-dev docker compose. I have OAuth configured with Okta. Nginix Proxy running in font of the HTTP container to perform SSL, which is functioning. Without OAuth, it works fine, with OAuth it perpetuates the 302 redirect issue. Authentication is good, user info is properly built upon return from Okta and I’m redirect to `/superset/welcome/` which 302’s me back to login as seen from output.

```bash
